From 9e3fdbb77849bbf3d9abc58643a3adfe7c24867b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:26:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/26] phy: mstar: add the MSC313 USB PHY with SSD20xD
 bring-up

Add the MStar MSC313 USB PHY (UTMI) driver from linux-chenxing, plus a
sstar,ssd20xd-usb-phy variant whose phy_init()/phy_power_on() replay the
vendor Titania3_series_start_ehc() UTMI/USBC sequence for SSD20xD byte
for byte. The vendor kernel shipped in the Gustard R26 contains exactly
this sequence (matched against the binary). The accesses are byte wide on
purpose: several hit the upper byte of a 16-bit RIU register next to
strobe bits.

Taken from the final state of the linux-chenxing mstar_v6_7_rebase branch
(https://github.com/linux-chenxing/linux, Daniel Palmer et al.) and ported
to v7.3. The VBUS enable result is now checked.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
